  "summary_md": "Today’s furnishings batch captures an industry still navigating soft housing and remodeling demand, but company-level narratives diverge sharply between cyclical resilience and radical strategic pivots. On the positive side, LCUT points to improving demand and market-share gains, while FLXS has consistently outgrown the industry and earned a Strong-Buy upgrade. The most transformational event is AMWD’s pending MasterBrand acquisition, introducing integration risk alongside housing-recovery upside. At the other extreme, SNBR remains under severe pressure with lingering liquidity concerns despite a product reboot.\n\nA striking cross-current is the number of micro-cap names abandoning legacy businesses for unproven ventures in AI, critical minerals, and energy infrastructure—XWIN, ATER, MWYN, EFOI—often accompanied by promotional coverage or outright sell ratings. Elsewhere, capital-allocation stories range from debt-free ETD’s steady dividend to buybacks at LOVE and FLXS, while one-time tariff benefits at COOK and HBB add noise to underlying trends.",
